# Rust
/target/
# `cmd/cargo-rivet`'s fixture crates are deliberately NOT workspace members —
# they are driven the way somebody else's crate would be — so the anchored
# `/target/` above does not cover them.
cmd/cargo-rivet/tests/fixtures/*/target/
# `tools/qemu/testapp` is its own workspace root for the same reason — it stands
# in for somebody else's application (ADR-017 §4's second origin), so it is
# built the way one would be.
tools/qemu/testapp/target/
# And so are the two `ADR-041` §8.4 fixtures — a virtual Bluetooth controller
# and a consumer that will not read — for the same reason.
tools/qemu/vhci-fixture/target/
tools/qemu/ble-backpressure/target/
# `tools/qemu/cpu-spin-probe` is its own workspace root too — it stands in for
# a SYSTEM service (`rivet-timed` or `rivet-bluetoothd`), not a workspace
# member, for `testapp`'s reason.
tools/qemu/cpu-spin-probe/target/
# **`cargo rivet package` writes beside the CRATE, not beside the workspace.**
# It is run from a member crate's own directory and emits into `<crate>/target/
# rivet/`, which the anchored `/target/` above does not reach — so packaging any
# workspace member for a board leaves an untracked target tree under `cmd/`,
# and a `git add -A` after one sweeps several hundred build files into a commit.
# That happened on 2026-09-16, packaging `rivet-fleetd` for `ADR-056`'s button.
cmd/*/target/
examples/*/target/
examples/*/*/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Image build output — generated, never committed
/build/
/out/
/rootfs/
*.img
*.img.xz
# Signed packages — ADR-029's container, in any of its three kinds. A build
# product like the card image beside it, and `cargo rivet package` writes one
# into a target directory by default.
*.rvt
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.ext4

# Vendored binaries and blobs — fetched by the build, not tracked.
# The Broadcom firmware and the Raspberry Pi boot firmware are redistributable
# but are not this project's to carry.
#
# **`/vendor/` IS NOT IGNORED WHOLESALE, AND MUST NOT BECOME SO.** Since
# 2026-09-04 it also holds `vendor/ixr-smb-server` — SOURCE this project owns
# and tracks (`.rulings/` R-134, and `VENDORING.md` beside it). Every rule below
# names one subdirectory on purpose. A future `/vendor/` line would silently
# untrack an adopted crate and its two signing fixes, and the failure would look
# like a clean checkout that does not build.
/vendor/firmware/
/vendor/boot/
/vendor/kernel/
# The C mechanisms Buildroot builds (ADR-009 §6) — BusyBox, `wpa_supplicant`
# and git. `cmd/rivet-image` takes each as a
# path argument rather than from a fixed directory, so nothing *requires* this
# one to exist; it is here because `vendor/bin` is the obvious place to put a
# half-megabyte static binary while working, and `AGENTS.md` §8.3's rule binds
# history rather than the working tree. A backstop, not the plan.
/vendor/bin/

# Provisioning files carry credentials. Zero-scrub (AGENTS.md §8.3) says these
# must never reach history; this is the backstop, not the plan.
rivet.local.toml
*.psk
*.nvram
*_rsa
*_ed25519
*.pem
*.key
*.seed

# Host tooling
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# QEMU loop inputs — somebody else's binaries, large, ADR-026 §6
tools/qemu/kernel8.img
tools/qemu/*.dtb
tools/qemu/*.cpio.gz

# Agent worktrees and local session state — never committed.
/.claude/
# Buildroot. `tools/buildroot/build.sh` defaults both the source tree and the
# output directory to $HOME precisely so these entries never have to fire — a
# toolchain and a kernel tree are several gigabytes and are `ADR-026` §6's
# inputs rather than this repository's artefacts. This is the backstop for

# somebody pointing RIVET_BR_OUTPUT or RIVET_BUILDROOT inside the tree,
# not the plan.
tools/buildroot/output/
tools/buildroot/dl/
tools/buildroot/buildroot-*/
tools/buildroot/**/Image
tools/buildroot/**/*.dtb

# HDMI captures of hardware experiments. 75 MB and growing; the console
# transcripts that matter are quoted into docs/ (ADR-018 §5.3.2, ADR-029 §9.3).
# Kept beside the repo, never in it.
/evidence/

# Python bytecode from tools/ (tools/qemu/interactive.py). Nothing on a card
# runs Python; these are a development instrument.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# **Scratch for the QEMU harness's --state, --libraries and --trust.** Seeded by
# hand; none of it is source. The libraries are copies out of the Buildroot
# sysroot and the trust store is extracted from a card image (PLAN.md §104.27.2)
# -- that one especially must never be committed, since the store that matters
# is the one cmd/rivet-image writes at build.
.qemu-state/
.qemu-libs/
.qemu-endpoints/
.qemu-aura/
trust-store.bin

# The renderer is cross-compiled by deploy/aura/renderer/build.sh, not cargo,
# and the binary lands beside the manifest to be packaged.
deploy/aura/renderer/aura-renderer

# Scratch pulled off the board while diagnosing. Never source.
*.tmp.json

# **Superseded 2026-09-04 — the manifest moved to `deploy/launcher/Cargo.toml`
# and is TRACKED.** This line is what made it untracked, which `.rulings/` R-138
# turned from untidy into dangerous: `connects = ["rivet-sysd:kiosk"]` is what
# tells the supervisor the launcher is the display arbiter rather than a lessee,
# and losing it costs the screen with nothing in the tree to say why. Kept so a
# checkout that still has the old scratch directory does not offer it back.
.launcher-pkg/
# The stripped cross-built launcher, staged beside its packaging manifest so
# `cargo rivet package --binary` can reach it — `deploy/aura/renderer` above,
# same reason. Reproducible from `cargo build -p rivetos-launcher`.
deploy/launcher/rivet-launcher
deploy/launcher/target/

# `cmd/rivet-proxyd/out/` — the stripped cross-built binary, staged there so
# `cargo rivet package --binary` can reach it from Windows. Reproducible.
cmd/rivet-proxyd/out/
.oldlauncher/
